# Claude dispatch

Claude leaders use separate planner/senior-dev subagents; senior-dev only on
explicit per-task choice. Send task/role/pass/baseline/patch, not parent history.
Preserve transcripts only if exported. Other harnesses require a verified,
approved mechanism before claiming native Claude planning/implementation.

Cross-tool Claude review is explicit and consent-gated. Configured claude/<id>
primary/fallback review uses this bounded wrapper, never oc.sh:

```bash
.agent-pipeline/bin/claude-review.sh --model claude/<id> \
  --prompt-file .agent-pipeline/prompts/T-<id>/reviewer-<pass>.md \
  --raw-out .agent-pipeline/logs/T-<id>/reviewer-<pass>.jsonl
```

At spec approval explain external account/billing/project guidance/hooks; record
Claude review approved: on only after consent. If only these catalog ids are
unchecked, obtain explicit human confirmation of exact model/runtime assignment
and record manual verification; invalid/unreachable other ids still block.
Audit existing hooks/settings first: Read/Grep/Glob restrictions do not disable
hook commands or provide OS isolation. Never bypass normal trust/permissions.

Use host background notifications or bounded foreground wrapper; bg-dispatch
is OpenCode-only. Wrapper retains transcript and validates session/model/verdict.
Record backend/model/session in the reviewer row; resume with --session only for
matching task/model and confirmed inactivity. Changed model means fresh review.
Never use lead/implementer session. Lead persists full findings unchanged, sets
Latest handoff, verifies state, branches on exact VERDICT line. Claude-authored
work needs a different-family reviewer; another harness is not independent weights.
